WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.830
- [Narrator] Should a
flood hit, Japan is ready.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:03.920
And their solution

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.680
is the largest underground
water facility in the world.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.680
(mellow electronic dance music)

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.110
About an hour outside of Tokyo

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.660
is the Metropolitan Area

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.763
Outer Underground Discharge Channel.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.910
This tunnel sits 160 feet underground,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.240
and is around 4 miles in length.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.030
Inside is a network of
large vertical shafts

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.373
that store flood waters.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.340
The giant tunnels were built

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.830
because this area of Japan

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.030
was constantly flooding.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.700
Now, instead of inundating nearby towns,

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.200
the water flows underground

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.570
and is diverted to a river

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:45.750
that can handle the influx of water,

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.400
making sure more than nine
million residents stay dry.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.400
(mellow electronic dance music)

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.897
(ding)

